I found out about this the hard way too.  I could list it under the
"luckiest, crawling-on-my-hands-and-knees almost-dead-on-my-last-hit-
point win of all time."

I was on the final level.  I had been blinded by something.  Don't know what.
I applied my unicorn horn.  But some sneaky Lich had cursed it!  After I
applied the horn I noticed I was still blind.  So what did I do?  I kept
applying it.  After about 5 turns I realized my mistake.  By now I'm
sick (from poison), hallucinating, stunned, confused and weak from hunger.
I stumbled onward; my ring of conflict kept the baddies busy while I ran
for cover.

On my last breath I decide to look down to see what's there.  Lo and behold!
It's an Altar!  And it's CROM's altar!  I quickly offered it up and *POOF* -
I'm immortal.

A few turns later I'd have been a corpse.

I defy anyone to win by such a slim margin.

